From 1e60926adcc904e844df7e96e7d2c5909443bbc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:01:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: composite the GUI over HDR only when the GUI
 pass drew into it

CompositeGui() takes the GUI FBO for empty from GetGUIElementCount(), the
count of the whole frame, which it reads after RenderEx(). RenderEx() draws
the bitmap subtitles of an HDR video (the PGS of a PQ stream) onto the
window's buffer, after the picture and outside the FBO
(CRenderer::RenderHDROverlays()), and COverlayTextureGLES::Render() counts
each of them as a GUI element. With a subtitle on screen and nothing of the
GUI, the empty FBO was taken for one that holds something: it was cleared at
the start of every frame and composited over the whole window at its end, a
full-screen clear and a full-screen pass of the composite shader in every
frame for as long as the subtitle stayed. The rule is Kodi's (its HDR
composite of the GUI). On an integrated GPU left at its own clock (the
COMPUTE power profile is set only while the Dolby Vision bridge draws) that
can make frames late.

The count that says what the FBO holds is the one of the GUI pass:
EndGuiComposite() takes it, before RenderEx(), and CompositeGui() decides by
it. The FBO is cleared and composited exactly when the GUI drew into it; the
subtitle is drawn as before. The same bytes reach the display: the composite
of an empty FBO discards every fragment. Native Dolby Vision output draws
these subtitles into its picture, which marks the frame as drawn over by
itself (BeginDVBridgeHDROverlays()); its frames with a subtitle and no GUI no
longer take the empty composite either, nor count as frames whose GUI the
packer composited.

Tests (outside the tree): pgs_composite_test, a model of the frame (a still
subtitle, one that comes and goes, the OSD over it and closing, the GUI pass
left out), where the old rule and two mutants fail; pgs_composite_wiring.py,
the order of the frame and the rule in the real code (fails on the tree
before); pgs_frame, the frames on llvmpipe and zink with Kodi's composite
shader at 3840x2160, full and limited range: the same bytes in the window
and in the FBO, and with a still subtitle 13.8 ms a frame instead of 33.9 on
llvmpipe (12.7 without a subtitle).
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h   | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
index 15a509e..eb0ca94 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -2149,6 +2149,9 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::BeginGuiComposite(bool guiWillRender)
 
 void CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::EndGuiComposite()
 {
+  // Hades: what the GUI pass drew into the FBO, before RenderEx() draws onto the window's buffer
+  // (CompositeGui())
+  m_guiPassElements = m_guiWillRender ? GetGUIElementCount() : 0;
   if (m_guiWillRender)
     m_guiFbo.EndRender();
 
@@ -2193,7 +2196,11 @@ void CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::CompositeGui()
   //   D2P:          "FBO is empty/clean AND back buffer cache is invalid"
   if (m_guiWillRender)
   {
-    const bool guiEmpty = (GetGUIElementCount() == 0);
+    // Hades: the elements of the GUI pass, which is what the FBO holds (EndGuiComposite()), not
+    // those of the whole frame: a bitmap subtitle of an HDR video is drawn by RenderEx() onto the
+    // window's buffer and counted as well, so that a subtitle on screen had the FBO, empty, cleared
+    // and composited over the whole window in every frame
+    const bool guiEmpty = (m_guiPassElements == 0);
     m_guiFboClean = guiEmpty;
     m_guiSeen = true; // (Hades: the FBO holds what this frame drew, and says if it is empty)
     if (guiEmpty)
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
index 9e24bcf..335d658 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
@@ -484,6 +484,11 @@ private:
   int m_guiFboHeight{0};
   // True when the GUI FBO is empty (no draws this frame); CompositeGui skips composite when true.
   bool m_guiFboClean{false};
+  //! Hades: the elements that the GUI pass of this frame drew into the FBO, counted where it ends
+  //! (EndGuiComposite()): GetGUIElementCount() is the count of the whole frame, and at
+  //! CompositeGui() it also counts what RenderEx() drew since onto the window's buffer (the bitmap
+  //! subtitles of an HDR video, OVERLAY::CRenderer::RenderHDROverlays())
+  unsigned int m_guiPassElements{0};
   // Whether the GUI render pass will run this frame; set by BeginGuiComposite.
   bool m_guiWillRender{true};
   //! Hades: the GUI pass of this frame is left out and its GUI is the FBO of the frame before
